==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Karasu-Tengu Tenten・Solution''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Tenten is what happens when you crank [[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Flight Unit R.E.I.]] to 11. For starters, a level 30 Tenten has more than 10k DPS, translating to a whole 40k against Floating with the related [[Fruit Treasures]]. For comparison, [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Windy α]] and Flight Unit R.E.I. have 20k and 24k effective DPS respectively, and [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] has 28k base DPS disregarding [[Talents]]. With this much firepower, Tenten can terrorize any Floating enemy unable to outrange her, moreso with a relatively good [[Freeze]] uptime. Unfortunately for her, she has three massive faults: extreme speed, an irritatingly long foreswing, and an unimpressive HP bracket. An aggressively supported [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]] or a hoard of [[Brollow]]s will have a laughably easy time exploiting these flaws and ripping her apart, as opposed to the vastly bulkier R.E.I. Tenten at least has a cooldown just lower than R.E.I.'s, so replacing her isn't too difficult. Using Tenten for generalist purposes, too, isn't a bad idea at all, assuming her speed can be worked around.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Crowd-Controller}}

